quran[13]{c,v,t}:
  72,1,"Say: ‘It has been revealed to me that a group of the jinn listened (to my recitation) and said (to their fellow jinn): ‘Indeed, we have heard a wonderful Qur’an."
  72,2,"It guides towards righteousness. So, we have believed in it, and we will never ascribe any partner to our Lord."
  72,3,And exalted be the Majesty of our Lord. He has not taken (for Himself) a spouse or a child.
  72,4,"Indeed, the foolish among us used to utter falsehoods about Allah."
  72,5,"And indeed, we had thought that no human or jinn would (dare to) tell a lie about Allah."
  72,6,"Some persons among the humans used to seek refuge with some persons of the jinn, so they further increased in rebellion."
  72,7,"And they (i.e. the humans) thought as you (jinn) thought, that Allah would never raise anyone (from the dead)."
  72,8,We tried to reach heaven (for news) but found it filled with mighty guards and shooting flames.
  72,9,"We used to sit in some of its sitting places to listen, but whoever dares to listen now finds a flame waiting for him."
  72,10,We do not know whether any evil is intended for those upon the earth or whether their Lord intends any good for them.
  72,11,"Among us, some are righteous, and among us, some are otherwise; we are divided into different paths."
  72,12,"We know that we can never escape Allah upon the earth, nor can we escape Him by flying (off the planet)."
  72,13,"When we heard the (message of) guidance, we believed in it. So, whoever believes in his Lord shall neither fear detraction nor oppression."
